  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6c3d3cc6-15df-5426-bea8-6fb57c7ec772" activityNameId="04b6857d-4054-5963-848b-bdd2187c5969" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ash horse dung and wood chips, to sanitary landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ash horse dung and wood chips, to sanitary landfill
Inventoried waste contains . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O n.a.; O 490900; H n.a.; C 12000; S 9200; N n.a.; P 3920; B n.a.; Cl 204; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 6.7; Ba n.a.; Cd 5; Co 1.8; Cr 19.5; Cu 103; Hg 0.01; Mn 20000; Mo 3.7; Ni 5.52; Pb 16; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V 39.5; Zn 1020; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti 1380; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 82600; Fe 22800; Ca 284000; Al 20800; K 18860; Mg 32100; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 100%. Overall degradability of waste during 100 years: 5%.;; UUID: b4081076-e1f1-440b-8005-93e734a25c5c
Waste-specific short-term emissions to air via landfill gas incineration and landfill leachate. Burdens from treatment of short-term leachate (0-100a) in wastewater treatment plant (including WWTP sludge disposal in municipal incinerator). Long-term emissions from landfill to groundwater (after base lining failure).
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal, leachate collection system, treatment of leachate in municipal wastewater treatment plant.
Technology: Swiss municipal sanitary landfill for biogenic or untreated municipal waste ("reactive organic landfill"). Landfill gas and leachate collection system. Recultivation and monitoring for 150 years after closure.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b4081076-e1f1-440b-8005-93e734a25c5c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
